-- a narrowing type hint decodes the statistics and the values into different value spaces:
-- castColumn wraps the values around while the min/max Fields keep the raw physical value
-- (issue #118383), so the row group must not be skipped by a bound the output type cannot
-- even hold. narrow2 stores Int32 65541 and 70000, which read as UInt16 5 and 4464
5
1000
1001
OK
4464
1999
1998
OK
-- and when only one of the two bounds is unrepresentable the other one stops bounding the
-- row group as well: narrow4 stores Int32 3 and 65537, which read as UInt16 3 and 1, so its
-- decodable min of 3 would skip the very row group that holds the answer 1
1
2
2
OK
-- a UUID sort key: Parquet orders UUID statistics bytewise while ClickHouse compares the two
-- 64-bit halves in the opposite order (issue #118371), so the bytewise min/max neither bound
-- the row group nor even stay in order. uuid2 holds the true top-1 behind its bytewise min
00000000-0000-0002-0000-000000000005
00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000000a
00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000000a
OK
00000000-0000-0003-0000-00000000001e
00000000-0000-0001-0000-000000000014
00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000000a
OK
-- uuid3 is the same mismatch seen from the other side: its bytewise min is above its bytewise
-- max in ClickHouse order, which would be rejected as self-contradictory statistics
ffffffff-ffff-ffff-0000-000000000001
00000000-0000-0000-ffff-ffffffffffff
OK
